The files in this directory come from lzma1 0.6.1 by Filip Seman, https://github.com/xseman/lzma1, under the Apache
License 2.0 in LICENSE here. They are the sources of tag v0.6.1, commit fc19ffcd4022b37297760c5dfec9292edf5875cd,
which match the src folder of lzma1-0.6.1.tgz on npm. lzma1 ports them from XZ for Java (0BSD) by Lasse Collin and
Igor Pavlov.

archive-defuse carries a copy instead of depending on the npm package. lzma1 0.6.1 exports only its high-level API,
and archive-defuse drives the streaming LZMA and LZMA2 decoders and the raw encoder below it: it needs the input bytes
the data took and what follows it, and it restarts one encoder for each LZMA2 chunk it writes. lzma1 is also an ES
module only, and archive-defuse compiles to CommonJS for Node 18 and later.

Copied: crc32.ts, hash234.ts, hc4.ts, header.ts, lz-decoder.ts, lz-encoder.ts, lzma-coder.ts, lzma-decoder.ts,
lzma-encoder.ts, lzma-encoder-fast.ts, lzma2-decoder.ts, range-coder.ts, range-decoder.ts and range-encoder.ts.

archive-defuse changed them as follows.

In every file:
- Biome reformatted it to this package's style, with spaces for tabs and single quotes for double.
- Imports drop the ".js" suffix, since this package compiles to CommonJS.
- A first line names lzma1 0.6.1, its license and this NOTICE.

This package's lint rules forbid assigning to a parameter, so these functions copy the parameter into a local
variable first and work on the copy. The arithmetic is the same.
- hc4.ts: skip().
- lz-decoder.ts: repeat().
- lz-encoder.ts: fillWindow().
- lzma-encoder.ts: getNormalPrice() and getMatchedPrice() of the literal encoder, and encode() of the length encoder.
- lzma2-decoder.ts: readChunkHeader(), decodeProps() and copyUncompressed().
- range-decoder.ts: decodeDirectBits().
- range-encoder.ts: getBitTreePrice(), getReverseBitTreePrice(), encodeReverseBitTree() and encodeDirectBits().

In lzma-decoder.ts, the matched literal loop builds its mask with -bit where lzma1 writes (0 - bit). The lint rules
read 0 - x as a type conversion. Both give 0 or -1 for a bit.

In lzma-encoder.ts:
- The empty body of the loop in encode() holds a comment.
- The import of State from lzma-coder.ts is gone, since nothing in the file uses it and the compiler refuses unused
  imports.

In lzma-encoder-fast.ts:
- getNextSymbol() throws if no matches were read, where it used a non-null assertion.
- A chained assignment is now two assignments.

In lzma2-decoder.ts:
- The file defines INPUT_MARGIN itself instead of importing it from alone-decoder.ts, which this package does not
  copy. The value is lzma1's, 64.
- A private method, currentLzma(), returns the LZMA decoder or throws "LZMA2 chunk without properties". It replaces
  two non-null assertions.

crc32.ts, hash234.ts, header.ts, lzma-coder.ts, range-coder.ts have no changes beyond formatting, imports and the
first line.
